  "walkthroughs": [
    {
      "tag": "Formula",
      "h2": "Midpoint formula",
      "body_html": "<p>Midpoint of (x₁, y₁) and (x₂, y₂) = ((x₁+x₂)/2, (y₁+y₂)/2).</p><p>Just average the x's, then average the y's.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Worked Example",
      "h2": "Midpoint of (2, 4) and (6, 10)",
      "body_html": "<p>x: (2 + 6) ÷ 2 = 4.</p><p>y: (4 + 10) ÷ 2 = 7.</p><p>Midpoint = <strong>(4, 7)</strong>.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Negative Coords",
      "h2": "Working with negatives",
      "body_html": "<p>Midpoint of (-2, 3) and (6, -1):</p><p>x: (-2 + 6) ÷ 2 = 2.</p><p>y: (3 + (-1)) ÷ 2 = 1.</p><p>Midpoint = <strong>(2, 1)</strong>.</p>"
    }
  ],
